Tile 8.3: NIC drops and errors

Set the tile timeframe to Last 2 hours. The status rules are placeholders:

Status	Condition🔴 Critical	Drops ≥ 5% of packets and ≥ 1 drop/s, or any NIC errors
🟠 Warning	Drops ≥ 1% of packets and ≥ 0.5 drops/s
timeseries {drx = avg(dt.host.net.nic.packets.dropped_rx),
            dtx = avg(dt.host.net.nic.packets.dropped_tx),
            erx = avg(dt.host.net.nic.packets.errors_rx),
            etx = avg(dt.host.net.nic.packets.errors_tx),
            prx = avg(dt.host.net.nic.packets.rx),
            ptx = avg(dt.host.net.nic.packets.tx)},
           by:{dt.entity.host, dt.entity.network_interface}
| fieldsAdd dropRate = coalesce(arrayAvg(drx), 0) + coalesce(arrayAvg(dtx), 0),
            errRate  = coalesce(arrayAvg(erx), 0) + coalesce(arrayAvg(etx), 0),
            pktRate  = coalesce(arrayAvg(prx), 0) + coalesce(arrayAvg(ptx), 0)
| fieldsAdd dropPct = if(pktRate > 0, 100.0 * dropRate / pktRate, else: 0.0)
| filter (dropPct >= 1 and dropRate >= 0.5) or errRate > 0
| lookup [ fetch dt.entity.host | fields id, hostName = entity.name, tags ],
         sourceField: dt.entity.host, lookupField: id, prefix: "h."
| lookup [ fetch dt.entity.network_interface | fields id, nicName = entity.name ],
         sourceField: dt.entity.network_interface, lookupField: id, prefix: "n."
| expand tag = h.tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| fieldsAdd status = if((dropPct >= 5 and dropRate >= 1) or errRate > 0, "🔴 Critical", else: "🟠 Warning"),
            rank   = if((dropPct >= 5 and dropRate >= 1) or errRate > 0, 1, else: 2)
| fieldsAdd appHostNic = concat(apmid, " | ", coalesce(h.hostName, "host n/a"), " : ",
                                coalesce(n.nicName, dt.entity.network_interface))
| fields status, appHostNic,
         dropPct = round(dropPct, decimals:2), dropsPerSec = round(dropRate, decimals:2),
         errorsPerSec = round(errRate, decimals:2),
         dt.entity.host, dt.entity.network_interface, rank
| sort rank asc, dropPct desc
| fieldsRemove rank

Settings: hide the two ID columns but keep them in the query so Open with works. Set the No data message to "No Claims NIC drops above threshold".
Expected result: roughly the 19 interfaces at 1% or more, minus any below 0.5 drops/s. Interfaces on shared hosts repeat under each app.
Check: I haven't confirmed that dt.entity.network_interface is a fetchable entity type. The dimension exists, but if the lookup errors, delete that lookup and use the ID as the label.
Errors: all Claims hosts showed 0 errors, so that column should stay at 0.
Tile 8.4: TCP retransmissions by app

Set the tile timeframe to Last 2 hours. The status rules are placeholders:

Status	Condition🔴 Critical	Retransmissions ≥ 5% of packets sent
🟠 Warning	≥ 1% of packets sent

Apps need at least 100 packets/s of traffic to appear.

timeseries {re = avg(dt.process.network.packets.re_tx_aggr),
            tx = avg(dt.process.network.packets.tx)},
           by:{dt.entity.process_group_instance}
| fieldsAdd reRate = coalesce(arrayAvg(re), 0),
            txRate = coalesce(arrayAvg(tx), 0)
| lookup [ fetch dt.entity.process_group_instance | fields id, tags ],
         sourceField: dt.entity.process_group_instance, lookupField: id, prefix: "e."
| expand tag = e.tags
| filter startsWith(tag, "APMID:")
| fieldsAdd apmid = splitString(tag, "APMID:")[1]
| filter in(apmid, array($ClaimsApps))
| summarize processes = countDistinctExact(dt.entity.process_group_instance),
            reRate    = sum(reRate),
            txRate    = sum(txRate),
            by:{apmid}
| fieldsAdd retransPct = if(txRate > 0, 100.0 * reRate / txRate, else: 0.0)
| filter retransPct >= 1 and txRate >= 100
| fieldsAdd status = if(retransPct >= 5, "🔴 Critical", else: "🟠 Warning"),
            rank   = if(retransPct >= 5, 1, else: 2)
| fields status, apmid, processes,
         retransPct = round(retransPct, decimals:2),
         retransPerSec = round(reRate, decimals:2),
         txPerSec = round(txRate, decimals:0), rank
| sort rank asc, retransPct desc
| fieldsRemove rank
